=== the prod approval gate, asked three ways =========================
$ gh api repos/UVE-QA/aws-devops-sdet-demo/environments/prod \
    --jq '{bypass: .can_admins_bypass, rr: [.protection_rules[]
           | select(.type=="required_reviewers")
           | {prevent_self_review, reviewers: [.reviewers[].reviewer.login]}]}'
{
  "bypass": false,
  "rr": [ { "prevent_self_review": false, "reviewers": [ "UVE-QA" ] } ]
}

$ gh api .../actions/runs/31329925499/pending_deployments   -> [] (empty)
$ gh api .../actions/runs/31329925499/approvals             -> state "approved",
                                                               user UVE-QA,
                                                               environment prod

The empty pending_deployments was read TWICE, at t=10s and t=60s, and read as
"the gate never paused". It does not distinguish that from "already approved".
`approvals` does. The gate is fine; the instrument was the wrong one.

=== the price, from the job logs (not from the step's green check) ===
The pricing step is `continue-on-error` and cannot redden, so its check is not
evidence. These lines are.

$ gh api repos/UVE-QA/aws-devops-sdet-demo/actions/jobs/93288721501/logs \
    | grep -Ei "published cost|nothing to price|created:"
  34 created: 3 priced, 27 free, 4 not metered, 0 UNPRICED
published cost (COMPUTED ESTIMATE, $0.017217 .. $0.022735):
  https://demo.uveapp.net/cost/prod/31330844910-destroy.json

$ gh api repos/UVE-QA/aws-devops-sdet-demo/actions/jobs/93290439062/logs \
    | grep -Ei "published cost|nothing to price|created:"
  32 created: 3 priced, 25 free, 4 not metered, 0 UNPRICED
published cost (COMPUTED ESTIMATE, $0.052648 .. $0.0581):
  https://demo.uveapp.net/cost/stage/31331527775-destroy.json

20h's stage cycle, for the comparison: $0.0178 .. $0.0235, and
`32 created: 3 priced, 25 free, 4 not metered, 0 UNPRICED` — the same breakdown
to the digit. The difference is how long the environment stood.

